> A quantizer that can be checked by hand

For a nonconstant coordinate with fitting bounds low and high, the stored symbol is
floor(clamp((v-low)/(high-low)*255,0,255)+.5). The arithmetic is evaluated in double after
reading Float32 inputs and ranges. With bounds [0,1], queries -.2,.5,1.2 become 0,128,255;
the middle value decodes to Float32(128/255), approximately .5019608. Halfway normalized
values round upward. If high equals low, every query emits zero and dequantization returns
the constant range value. Clamping loses out-of-range information; the fitting range is not
expanded using test values.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/codec_toy_quantizer.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  const m::CodecQuantizer q{{0.f}, {1.f}};
  const auto              query   = n::tensor({-.2, .5, 1.2}, {3, 1});
  const auto              symbols = m::QuantizeCodec(query, q);
  const auto              decoded = m::DequantizeCodec(symbols, q);
  std::print("| query | symbol | decoded |\n|---:|---:|---:|\n");
  for (int i = 0; i < 3; ++i)
    std::print("| {:.1f} | {} | {:.9f} |\n", query.at({i, 0}), int(symbols[i]), decoded.at({i, 0}));
  auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.lines({-.3, 1.3}, {-.3, 1.3}, "Identity", {100, 116, 139}, 1.5)
      .points(
          query.to_vector<double>(), decoded.to_vector<double>(), "Byte inverse", {37, 99, 235}, 5.)
      .x_limits(-.3, 1.3)
      .y_limits(-.3, 1.7)
      .x_label("Original coordinate")
      .y_label("Decoded coordinate")
      .title("Explicit clipping and a half-up midpoint")
      .save_svg("build/codec_toy_quantizer.svg");
}
```
