> A separate program decodes without loading a dataset or encoder

This is a complete second receiver executable. It opens only the generated file, parses its
bounded structure and decodes from packet values. It saves reconstructed probabilities and
identities for a byte-exact comparison with the sender-side result. It neither instantiates
an encoder nor accesses the dataset cache.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <fstream>
#include <iterator>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::ifstream input("build/codec/test.tflcodec", std::ios::binary);
  if (!input)
    throw std::runtime_error("Open transmitted codec file");
  const std::vector<std::uint8_t> bytes((std::istreambuf_iterator<char>(input)), {});
  const auto                      packet  = n::models::UnpackCodec(bytes);
  const auto                      decoded = n::models::DecodeCodec(packet);
  n::save_npz(
      "build/codec/fresh_decoded.npz",
      {{"source_ids", n::from_vector(packet.source_ids, {std::int64_t(packet.source_ids.size())})},
       {"reconstruction", decoded}});
  std::print(
      "Decoded {} images from {} bytes; no encoder or dataset access.\n",
      packet.source_ids.size(),
      bytes.size());
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Decoded 200 images from 110972 bytes; no encoder or dataset access.
// result_end
> The teaching packet format is explicit

TFLCODE1 is a local fixed-architecture format, preserved for compatibility with the original
example. Unsigned integers and IEEE754 Float32 scalars are little endian. The five header
integers are N,32,28,28,1. Bounds are interleaved minimum/maximum pairs; decoder weights
are row-major [32,784], followed by 784 biases. Source identities precede N*32 payload bytes.
The parser accepts 1 through 10,000 images and exactly 103772+36*N bytes. Signed-zero float
bits survive serialization; every encoded parameter must be finite and every bound ordered.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/codec_packet_layout.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  dm::graphics::Diagram          d(48, 1300);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle s;
  s.width     = 7.4;
  s.height    = 3.2;
  s.font_size = 18;
  d.node("h", {0, 0}, "Header: 28 bytes\nMagic + N/32/28/28/1\nOffset 0", s)
      .node("q", {9, 0}, "Ranges: 256 bytes\n32 Float32 min/max pairs\nOffset 28", s)
      .node("w", {18, 0}, "Decoder: 103488 bytes\nW then bias, Float32\nOffset 284", s)
      .node("i", {27, 0}, "Identities: 4N bytes\nNonnegative Int32 IDs\nOffset 103772", s)
      .node("p", {36, 0}, "Symbols: 32N bytes\nRow-major byte codes\nOffset 103772+4N", s)
      .edge("h", "q")
      .edge("q", "w")
      .edge("w", "i")
      .edge("i", "p")
      .text(
          {18, -5},
          "Total = 103772 + 36N bytes. No checksum, entropy coding or encoder weights.",
          20)
      .save_svg("build/codec_packet_layout.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/codec_packet_layout.svg)
// result_end
\caption(All byte offsets are part of the checked format contract; the decoder overhead is transmitted once for this file.)
\alttext(A five-section packet with exact header, range, decoder, identity and payload offsets.)

> Payload rate and complete-file rate answer different questions

The 6,400 symbol bytes alone cost .326531 bits per pixel. The complete file costs 5.661837
bits per pixel, while the measured PNG collection costs 2.545357. Decoder overhead is amortized
over these actual 200 images. The figure below exposes the overhead before the rate comparison;
no imaginary corpus or payload-only rate replaces the full file. A coordinate count of 32 versus
784 by itself is not a compression-rate measurement.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/codec_byte_categories.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <fstream>
#include <iterator>
int main() {
  std::ifstream in("build/codec/test.tflcodec", std::ios::binary | std::ios::ate);
  if (!in)
    throw std::runtime_error("Open packet");
  const auto bytes = std::size_t(in.tellg());
  const auto n     = dm::nn::models::UnpackCodec([&] {
                   in.seekg(0);
                   return std::vector<std::uint8_t>((std::istreambuf_iterator<char>(in)), {});
                 }())
                     .source_ids.size();
  const std::vector<double> x{0, 1, 2, 3, 4},
      counts{28, 256, 103488, double(n * 4), double(n * 32)};
  if (bytes != 28 + 256 + 103488 + n * 36)
    throw std::runtime_error("Complete accounting");
  auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.bars(x, counts, "Stored bytes", dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235}, .7)
      .x_ticks(x, {"Header", "Ranges", "Decoder", "Identities", "Symbols"})
      .x_label("Every transmitted byte category")
      .y_label("Actual bytes")
      .title("The decoder dominates this complete file")
      .save_svg("build/codec_byte_categories.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/codec_byte_categories.svg)
// result_end
\caption(All five categories sum to the actual file length; the decoder contributes 103,488 bytes.)
\alttext(A complete byte accounting bar chart with a dominant decoder-weight bar and smaller payload, identity, range and header bars.)

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/codec_rates.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <fstream>
#include <iterator>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::ifstream in("build/codec/test.tflcodec", std::ios::binary);
  if (!in)
    throw std::runtime_error("Open packet");
  const std::vector<std::uint8_t> bytes((std::istreambuf_iterator<char>(in)), {});
  const auto                      packet = n::models::UnpackCodec(bytes);
  std::size_t                     png    = 0;
  for (int id : packet.source_ids)
    png += std::filesystem::file_size(
        std::filesystem::path("build/codec/original_png") / (std::to_string(id) + ".png"));
  const double              pixels = packet.source_ids.size() * 784.;
  const std::vector<double> x{0, 1, 2, 3};
  const std::vector<double> rates{
      packet.symbols.size() * 8 / pixels, bytes.size() * 8 / pixels, png * 8 / pixels, 8};
  auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.bars(x, rates, "Bits per pixel", dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235}, .65)
      .x_ticks(x, {"Symbols only", "Complete TFLCODE1", "Original PNGs", "Raw U8 pixels"})
      .x_label("Actual 200-image collection; PNG is lossless")
      .y_label("Stored bits / original pixel")
      .title("The complete learned file is larger than the measured PNG collection")
      .save_svg("build/codec_rates.svg");
}
```
