\image(figures/codec_rates.svg)
// result_end
\caption(PNG uses original lossless images; the learned result is lossy. Headers and actual complete-file overhead remain included as described.)
\alttext(Four rates compare symbol payload, complete codec, original PNG collection and raw pixels; the complete codec exceeds PNG.)

> Quantization error is small beside the learned reconstruction loss

The global test MSE uses all 156,800 pixel values. Global PSNR is 10 log10(1/MSE) for the fixed
unit pixel range; it is not the mean of per-image PSNR. Quantization slightly increases pixel
MSE here. The 32-code decoder’s reconstruction loss dominates that difference. There are three
constant fitting-code channels and nine out-of-range held-out code entries; these values are
retained in the archived diagnostics. No quality-success selection is applied.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/codec_distortion.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <map>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> a;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : n::load_npz("build/codec/analysis.npz"))
    a.emplace(k, v);
  const auto          truth = n::models::DoubleSampleRows(a.at("test_images"));
  std::vector<double> errors;
  for (const auto& key : {"unquantized_reconstruction", "decoded_reconstruction"})
    errors.push_back(n::mean(n::square(n::models::DoubleSampleRows(a.at(key)) - truth)).item());
  std::print("Additional pixel MSE after quantization: {:.12g}.\n", errors[1] - errors[0]);
  auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.bars({0, 1}, errors, "Test pixel MSE", dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235}, .6)
      .x_ticks({0, 1}, {"Unquantized autoencoder", "Packet decoder"})
      .x_label("Same fixed 200 held-out images")
      .y_label("Mean squared pixel error")
      .title("Post-training byte quantization barely changes a blurry decoder")
      .save_svg("build/codec_distortion.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Additional pixel MSE after quantization: 1.203498187e-06.
\image(figures/codec_distortion.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Both bars start at zero, showing that the quantization increment is small compared with total decoder reconstruction loss.)
\alttext(Unquantized and packet-decoded reconstruction errors are nearly equal around .0503.)

> Ten predetermined held-out cases, including failures

Rows use indices floor(k*199/9), k=0,...,9, exactly the original evenly spaced rule. Columns
are original image, unquantized autoencoder, file-decoded reconstruction and absolute decoded
pixel error. Images use fixed [0,1] grayscale with no per-image normalization; error uses that
same range and is not amplified. Source IDs and both per-case errors make the weak cases
traceable. Labels do not choose cases, fit ranges, enter the file or select the model.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/codec_cases.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <map>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> a;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : n::load_npz("build/codec/analysis.npz"))
    a.emplace(k, v);
  const auto truth = a.at("test_images").reshape({200, 784}),
             unq = a.at("unquantized_reconstruction"), decoded = a.at("decoded_reconstruction"),
             error              = n::abs(decoded - truth);
  const auto             source = a.at("test_source_ids").to_vector<int>();
  std::vector<n::Tensor> tiles;
  std::print("| row | source ID | unquantized MSE | decoded MSE |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n");
  for (int k = 0; k < 10; ++k) {
    const int  row      = k * 199 / 9;
    const auto original = n::take_rows(truth, {row});
    auto       mse      = [&](const n::Tensor& x) {
      return n::mean(
                 n::square(
                     n::cast(n::take_rows(x, {row}), n::DType::Float64) -
                     n::cast(original, n::DType::Float64)))
          .item();
    };
    std::print("| {} | {} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} |\n", row, source[row], mse(unq), mse(decoded));
    for (const auto& p : {truth, unq, decoded, error})
      tiles.push_back(n::take_rows(p, {row}).reshape({1, 28, 28, 1}));
  }
  n::save_image_grid(n::concat(tiles, 0), "build/codec_cases.png", 4, 0, 1, 4, 220. / 255., 3);
}
